CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*nn->conf_str_hashtbl)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct list_head)...)
#185: FILE: fs/nfsd/nfs4state.c:4751:
+	nn->conf_str_hashtbl = kmalloc(sizeof(struct list_head) *

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

CHECK:AVOID_EXTERNS: extern prototypes should be avoided in .h files
#222: FILE: fs/nfsd/state.h:486:
+extern int nfs4_has_reclaimed_state(const char *name, struct nfsd_net *);

Function prototypes don't need to be declared extern in .h
files.  It's assumed by the compiler and is unnecessary.

WARNING:FUNCTION_ARGUMENTS: function definition argument 'struct nfsd_net *' should also have an identifier name
#222: FILE: fs/nfsd/state.h:486:
+extern int nfs4_has_reclaimed_state(const char *name, struct nfsd_net *);

This warning is emitted due to any of the following reasons:

  1. Arguments for the function declaration do not follow
     the identifier name.  Example::

       void foo
       (int bar, int baz)

     This should be corrected to::

       void foo(int bar, int baz)

  2. Some arguments for the function definition do not
     have an identifier name.  Example::

       void foo(int)

     All arguments should have identifier names.

